{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1498830-paths-of-the-eightfold-wheel-and-watchful-gods","id":1498830,"title":"Paths of the Eightfold Wheel and Watchful Gods","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-12-05T03:35:40-08:00","id":1498830,"title":"Paths of the Eightfold Wheel and Watchful Gods","content":"V20 Dark Ages seems to add two additional Paths to the Road of Sin that are inspired by older pagan beliefs: The Path of the Eightfold Wheel (Druidic paganism) and the Path of Watchful Gods (Graeco-Roman paganism).<br /> <br /> In previews on the Onyx Path website, these paths were clearly listed under the Road of Heaven. However, the book lists them both under &quot;Other Paths&quot;, coming immediately after the Road of Sin and appearing as a subheading of that section in the table of contents. This seems like a mistake.<br /> <br /> The descriptions of the Road of Sin and Road of Heaven would lead to a reading in which they belong to the latter. For example, the entry for the Road of Heaven explicitly mentions these paths, while the entry for the Road of Sin does not.<br /> <br /> Hence, under the Road of Heaven, it says, &quot;These differing religious traditions inform how Cainites on the Road of Heaven make sense of their Embrace. [...] Druidic Cainites reason that serving the Great Balance requires darkness as well as light [describes the Path of the Eightfold Wheel]. And a servant of the old Roman Gods believes that she had somehow offended one of them and must strive to regain that god\u2019s favor [describes the Path of Watchful Gods].&quot; (Vampire: The Dark Ages 20th Anniversary Edition, p.119)<br /> <br /> The ethics of Sin clearly contradict the Hierarchy of Sins for both Paths, too, and the Road of Sins Virtues clearly seem like poor fits with these codes (although Conviction might fit Watchful Gods and Instinct might fit the Eightfold Wheel if you squint).<br /> <br /> So I think you can read this in either of two ways:<br /> <br /> 1. The Paths were moved to the Road of Sin late on, and the fluff wasn't updated to match this new placement, which is why the Road of Sin makes no mention to these Paths and doesn't really fit.<br /> <br /> OR<br /> <br /> 2. The Paths were pasted into the wrong place during editing or layout, and should have remained with the Road of Heaven. The section following these Paths, which talks about non-Abrahamic religions, seems a direct response to the Paths of Christ, Life and the Prophet, and so this may verify that intention.<br /> <br /> A third option is that &quot;Other Paths&quot; was supposed to indicate an entirely separate section, like the section on Minor Roads, to encompass Paths not under any Road at all. In that case, the Paths were in the right place, but because the wrong header style was used, the section was deprecated to look like a subheading of the Road of Sin instead of its own section, and this error was repeated in the table of contents.<br /> <br /> Have we, as far as we know, had any dev clarification on this issue? I can see there was a minor debate on the wiki about the issue, but it didn't seem anyone had a concrete answer to resolve it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-05T06:08:37-08:00","id":1498842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1498830-paths-of-the-eightfold-wheel-and-watchful-gods#post1498830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And a servant of the old Roman Gods believes that she had somehow offended one of them and must strive to regain that god\u2019s favor [describes the Path of Watchful Gods].&quot; (Vampire: The Dark Ages 20th Anniversary Edition, p.119)</div> </div> </div> </div>This Path sounds almost custom built for <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Thaddeus\" target=\"_blank\">one of the first characters of the game</a>.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-05T08:21:13-08:00","id":1498862,"title":"","content":"I tend to treat them as minor roads in their own right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"